mbda y=0,\\,y(0)=y(5)=0,\\,0\\le x\\le 5,\\,\\lambda \\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues and the associated eigenfunctions of this problem.$\\,$ The eigenvalues correspond to the parameter values ${\\lambda }_{n}=$ {{field-1}}, where $n\\in N.$\n\n$\\,$ The eigenfunctions are ${y}_{n}(x)=$ {{field-2}}, where ${B}_{n}\\in R.$" :question/worked-solution "We consider the cases $\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda >0$ separately, since they correspond to different solutions. \n\n**Case 1**: First, we consider $\\lambda =0.$ \n\nSetting $\\lambda =0$ gives the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=0.\n$$\n\nIntegrating this equation gives\n\n$$\ny=Ax+B.\n$$\n\nApplying the conditions $y(0)=y(5)=0$ yields the trivial solution $y≡0.$ Since the zero solution is not an eigenfunction, $\\lambda =0$ does not correspond to an eigenvalue.\n\n**Case 2**: Next, we consider $\\lambda >0.$\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we set $y={e}^{mx}.$ The auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}+16\\lambda  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $m=\\pm 4\\text{i}\\sqrt{\\lambda }.$ So, the fundamental solutions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x\\sqrt{\\lambda }),\\,{y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x\\sqrt{\\lambda })\n$$\n\nand the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x\\sqrt{\\lambda })+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x\\sqrt{\\lambda }).\n$$\n\nApplying the boundary condition $y(0)=0$ yields\n\n$$\nA\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)=0\n$$\n\nwhich gives $A=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\ny=B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x\\sqrt{\\lambda }).\n$$\n\nApplying the boundary condition $y(5)=0$ yields\n\n$$\nB\\operatorname{sin}⁡(20\\sqrt{\\lambda })=0.\n$$\n\nFor nontrivial solutions, we require \n\n$$\n20\\sqrt{\\lambda }=n\\pi \n$$\n\nfor $n\\in N.$ This gives the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues:\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{400}.\n$$\n\nThe corresponding eigenfunctions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{n}(x)={B}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{n}}),\\,{B}_{n}\\in R.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-338916/field-1" "q-338916/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "472cbb79-e22b-50d2-a997-93130ff66c22"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338916"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338921/field-1/d2386f85ac8e151e7707e6ff9f719bac1cb7a58183beaa15a6eb998c12daddd6" :answer/id #uuid "1c14b9ee-e58f-516c-a1a3-195c750de2e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{n}^{2}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338921/field-1/f2792d885a1a6be1d201f76fb64b038f099a60a6449a7fc395f53c83dc5b250f" :answer/id #uuid "c62f2b00-4f47-52db-969d-136479e33863" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{n}^{2}}{50}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338921/field-1/c02de963dc19dda281f66148b2f2329119265c0e8cd62bbf9522f261d93c109b" :answer/id #uuid "4ed42872-9fbb-5c01-8ee4-255df2140180" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{n}^{2}}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338921/field-1/07c0a6a6dae50c18ebde5d37d22093658c9770907bd21f6b624043557f5985d5" :answer/id #uuid "8bedc359-7d2a-5f82-9f14-82db352d3d0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{n}^{2}}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338921/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "169b79ce-78f5-5ef8-9444-bf12ad43c40b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-338921/field-1/c02de963dc19dda281f66148b2f2329119265c0e8cd62bbf9522f261d93c109b" :answer-field/choices ["q-338921/field-1/d2386f85ac8e151e7707e6ff9f719bac1cb7a58183beaa15a6eb998c12daddd6" "q-338921/field-1/f2792d885a1a6be1d201f76fb64b038f099a60a6449a7fc395f53c83dc5b250f" "q-338921/field-1/c02de963dc19dda281f66148b2f2329119265c0e8cd62bbf9522f261d93c109b" "q-338921/field-1/07c0a6a6dae50c18ebde5d37d22093658c9770907bd21f6b624043557f5985d5"] :db/ensure [:answer-f